    <section class="essay-section" id="the-limit">
      <h2 class="section-label">Where the Framework Met Its Limit</h2>
      <p>
        Each partner organization reported on 10 to 25 metrics. That's
        reasonable for an organization with a dedicated data person. Many
        partner organizations didn't have one.
      </p>
      <p>
        The measurement work landed on program managers who were simultaneously
        running programs and supervising staff. The framework assumed a
        staffing reality the partners didn't have, and the gap wasn't funded.
        Partners were asked to provide data without the capacity to produce it
        well.
      </p>
      <p>
        They also weren't in the reflection sessions where the backbone was
        making sense of the data they helped produce. The people closest to the
        communities being served were generating the raw material for analysis
        they didn't participate in.
      </p>

