    <section class="essay-section" id="building-today">
      <h2 class="section-label">If I Were Building This Today</h2>
      <p>The answer goes bigger than the evaluation structure.</p>
      <p>
        First, diversify the funding base. Single-funder dependency drove the
        scope of the framework. Trust-based, capacity-building foundations make
        it possible to right-size the measurement ask instead of inflating it.
      </p>
      <p>
        Second, cut the measurement ask. One to two outcome-level indicators
        per partner organization, plus one to three deep qualitative check-ins
        per year. That's where the real learning lives. Outputs measured as
        outputs. Outcomes measured as outcomes.
      </p>
      <p>
        Third, fund partner data capacity as part of the program budget, not as
        an unfunded assumption that program managers will absorb.
      </p>
      <p>
        Fourth, redefine the backbone's role. Capacity-building and partner
        inclusion in the reflection process. Not compliance management.
      </p>
    </section>

    <hr class="rule" />

    <div class="coda">
      <p>
        The framework outran the funding because the funding asked it to.
        Build differently, and it doesn't have to.
      </p>
